  "steps": [
   "The scheduler starts the batch after XD12 has finished successfully (job chain XD12 -> XD11 -> XD08). Write LOG1.",
   "Select the lines (CUSTOMER_CD + CUSTOMER_ORDER_NO + ORDER_DT + ORDER_TIME + DESTINATION_CD + DETAILED_ITEM_NO) that have rows with ORDER_STATUS = '2' and CANCEL_STATUS = 'P' in TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CONTROL_PRE. Read all rows of these lines (every SERIAL_NO).",
   {
    "text": "For each line, compute the line figures (see Line Figures):",
    "children": [
     "CANCEL_QTY (status 2 rows 'P'), VALID_QTY (status 7 + 6 rows), QTY_IN_ASN and QTY_OPEN from TB_R_INSTRUCTION."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Release the open mapping of the line (when QTY_OPEN > 0):",
    "children": [
     "Delete the rows of the line in TB_R_INSTRUCTION without ASN_NO. A Case List still open for these rows can no longer be submitted (the submit fails; the user creates the ASN again).",
     "Reduce MAPPED_QTY in TB_R_PRA_DAILY_ORDER_MAPPED by the qty of the deleted rows, per PO part.",
     "Set PO_MAPPED_FLAG = 'N' on the status 7 rows of the line that have no row left in TB_R_INSTRUCTION: their valid qty is pre-mapped again by the next XD09 run.",
     "Rows with ASN_NO (submitted ASN) are never changed."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Judge the result (see Result Rule):",
    "children": [
     "CANCELLED: QTY_IN_ASN <= VALID_QTY. Write LOG3.",
     "CONFLICT: QTY_IN_ASN > VALID_QTY; CONFLICT_QTY pcs were shipped (or will be) without order. Write LOG4."
    ]
   },
   "Set CANCEL_STATUS = 'D' on the processed status 2 rows and insert one record per row in TB_R_CROSSDOCK_CANCEL_RESULT (with the line figures). Commit per line: an error stops only this line (LOG5); its rows stay 'P' and are processed by the next run.",
   "More lines: back to step 3. Else write LOG2 (counts per result). Exit."
  ]
 },
